#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186601922 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14a7fad8-1ccc-5361-ae99-fadb75dd082a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186601609} {:answer/id #uuid "75edf9a9-a86f-5628-b440-ed9fcdbce477" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186601684} {:answer/id #uuid "9a86bf81-459b-5402-8475-4671fdd39669" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186601717} {:answer/id #uuid "ab7313e7-9c7c-5d4f-aa15-2d639dd58975" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186601729} {:answer/id #uuid "f9b6fd80-6441-5406-8fbe-9719cf74651a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186601807}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186601807} :answer-field/id #uuid "264078c2-360f-5a55-9a1d-47f10d85e767" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186601825}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7663d433-7983-5195-82f9-f8b3b6b0d6aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-79350" :question/problem "Find $\\text{rank}(A)$ given that\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}-{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=5,$ since this is the number of components in each of the vectors of the null space. \n\nAlso, since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that $\\text{nullity}(A)=3.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+3 & =5 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =5-3 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186601938 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05f5fb18-cd10-50a1-804b-52cc7bd09f49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186601603} {:answer/id #uuid "34213afb-951e-586a-910f-32f76d572451" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186601633} {:answer/id #uuid "4b033259-ad61-5852-b7ae-4c69d95eadda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186601649} {:answer/id #uuid "be45a3e2-f6af-5a5c-8b30-6476c2da97d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186601756} {:answer/id #uuid "f135b625-3a56-594d-83f9-4191b8a5a9e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186601795}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186601795} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c2ff09e-a029-5cda-a90b-ac45f62f8970" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186601827}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "c935622f-4794-551b-bc04-e73546072768" :question/math-academy-id "q-35424" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and  $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{1} \\\\ -5{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1}\\in R\\}?$ \n\nI. $\\text{rank}(A)=3$\n\nII. $A$ is invertible\n\nIII. $det(A)=0$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{3} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=3=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$  \n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{1} \\\\ -5{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1}\\in R\\}=\\text{Span}\\{\\,\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}\\}\n$$\n\n \nwe have that $\\text{nullity}(A)=1.$\n\nNow,  for the matrix $A,$ the number of columns is $n=3,$ so according to the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+1 & =3 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =3-1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{nullity}(A)=1\\ne 0,$ then by the invertible matrix theorem, $A$ can't be an invertible matrix.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since $A$ is not invertible we must have   $det(A)=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186602424 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "098ef7d9-5769-58ae-a335-036b70249ce5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -2 & -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602059} {:answer/id #uuid "1c9b3d92-3824-5e10-a4f4-49aa1e897ae5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 2 & -7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602081} {:answer/id #uuid "2b34a625-bed6-57f1-a30a-3b1b1ed1a1ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 & -9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602097} {:answer/id #uuid "2e218715-4362-559c-bf01-ebc771eab4ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 3 & -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602101} {:answer/id #uuid "e0b20ff9-8b7c-5596-8865-3506ac664436" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 2 & -8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602274}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186602081} :answer-field/id #uuid "36212398-c0ed-51a3-a332-208b9342eead" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602325}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "75b40f52-40d8-537f-b6a5-8648a574261a" :question/math-academy-id "q-129497" :question/problem "If\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand\n$$\n\\displaystyle B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nthen $AB=$" :question/worked-solution "Here, $A$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix and $B$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix. \n\nThere are $2$ columns in $A$ and $2$ rows in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 3}={AB}_{1\\times 3}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,9=2\\cdot 3+3\\cdot 1 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 2 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,2=2\\cdot (-2)+3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 2 & -7\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-7=2\\cdot 1+3\\cdot (-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$$\n\\displaystyle AB=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 2 & -7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186602432 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15ce3df2-98e6-5489-819f-57c6085b93e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}12 & 16 \\\\ -3 & -4 \\\\ -9 & 12\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602073} {:answer/id #uuid "86ab563b-b5af-579f-9da5-ea3119739354" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "Undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602175} {:answer/id #uuid "e79f5764-48a0-5eee-9604-ef229a4b4b8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}12 & 16 \\\\ -3 & -4 \\\\ 9 & -12\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602280} {:answer/id #uuid "edb48f97-2872-5bc2-90e7-1bfd2370f84a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}12 & 16 \\\\ -3 & -4 \\\\ -9 & -12\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602284} {:answer/id #uuid "f61e715b-3887-57d6-845a-2c78de19b972" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}12 & -16 \\\\ -3 & -4 \\\\ -9 & -12\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602297}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186602284} :answer-field/id #uuid "bde6bb3c-ac7e-5195-ade2-fb4da3537af8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602374}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "89309542-99aa-554d-a4b0-3e012ff29ce3" :question/math-academy-id "q-13645" :question/problem "Find $ST$, if \n$$\n\\displaystyle S=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand \n$$\n\\displaystyle T=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Here, $S$ is $3\\times 1$ matrix and $T$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in $S$ and $1$ row in $T$, so the product is well defined:\n\n$$\n{S}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{T}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={ST}_{3\\times 2}\n$$\n\nComputing the product, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ST & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4\\cdot 3 & 4\\cdot 4 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot 3 & (-1)\\cdot 4 \\\\ (-3)\\cdot 3 & (-3)\\cdot 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}12 & 16 \\\\ -3 & -4 \\\\ -9 & -12\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186602444 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9703f8e-5cf3-58d8-b084-47a0b792e47b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602251}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186602251} :answer-field/id #uuid "71c42643-0393-5573-888c-09b8ce398c19" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602343} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20b56970-6bb5-5108-bb2c-77dc54c74421" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602085}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186602085} :answer-field/id #uuid "df3ff047-72be-5ef1-9b5a-2edc81025a9a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602385}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d1702e86-c34d-50db-922d-80c8b5e93cb8" :question/math-academy-id "q-318413" :question/problem "Determine $AB$ given that \n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand\n$$\n\\displaystyle B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"1\">$AB=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Here, $A$ is a $1\\times 3$ matrix and $B$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $A$ and $3$ rows in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}={AB}_{1\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet’s compute the entries of $AB,$ one at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-10=(-2)\\cdot 3+0\\cdot 5+1\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 2\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,2=(-2)\\cdot (-1)+0\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nAB=\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186602458 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17a74bb1-22c0-54a4-a64e-76568f21d532" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 \\\\ 12 & 16 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602075} {:answer/id #uuid "334b2c36-174f-5275-a2ed-708c07636247" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 \\\\ 16 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602106} {:answer/id #uuid "496ce67e-ec54-5459-99d3-0bf5e49789eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "Undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602121} {:answer/id #uuid "6fc4b612-768f-507c-892d-84064e614c90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 12 & 16 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602149} {:answer/id #uuid "b656c562-5679-5424-bc0a-3e4df0169489" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 16 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602229}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186602075} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3959ad8-c1f3-55ee-8d80-1d17d8e57051" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602375}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f6d079c7-be62-585e-a415-433f8bab1c90" :question/math-academy-id "q-130184" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Here, the first factor is $3\\times 1$ matrix and the second factor is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in the first matrix and $1$ row in the second matrix, so the product is well defined:\n\n$$\n3\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}✓\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2=3\\times 2\n$$\n\nComputing the product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1\\cdot 3 & 1\\cdot 4 \\\\ 4\\cdot 3 & 4\\cdot 4 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot 3 & (-1)\\cdot 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 \\\\ 12 & 16 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186605092 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fa3c442-9bc5-521d-a8bd-6505aec65de1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=-1,\\,c=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604776} {:answer/id #uuid "5f8b6566-57ca-5aef-add4-a94633db29ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=0,\\,b=1,\\,c=-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604829} {:answer/id #uuid "72d902c5-3e86-51b1-8735-4c6e424c78ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=-4,\\,b=-1,\\,c=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604852} {:answer/id #uuid "94feec58-3996-59b8-aeb8-a5d0061d3999" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=0,\\,b=-1,\\,c=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604887} {:answer/id #uuid "bb117bf1-4f82-50a5-99df-195d798d5dbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=-1,\\,c=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604934}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604887} :answer-field/id #uuid "d597f0ad-6ebf-57e9-969f-84c287162e74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186605071}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "298cf9b8-ec08-5ea6-bf84-6c375b81fb49" :question/math-academy-id "q-36186" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x-4y &=3+z \\\\ y &=2+z \\\\ -y+5x-9 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -4 & -1 \\\\ a & 1 & b \\\\ 5 & c & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x-4y-z &=3 \\\\ 0x+y-z &=2 \\\\ 5x-y+0z &=9\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=0,\\,b=-1,\\,c=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186605117 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01fad31f-f5d6-5d6e-97fc-bbcfe448f808" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "${D}^{-1}$ and $s$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604734} {:answer/id #uuid "64e44511-47a7-551f-bbe8-9ca1923f35de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$D$ and ${I}_{n}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604837} {:answer/id #uuid "afacdc5a-00e6-5372-a4ad-e68eb6dc0fbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "${I}_{n}$ and $s$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604917} {:answer/id #uuid "c977a6a5-5791-5c37-8f21-79f266b32212" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "${I}_{n}$ and ${I}_{n}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604950} {:answer/id #uuid "d4a3a53d-c8f5-517d-96ba-21e83348a198" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$D$ and $s$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604961}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604917} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9828008-405d-55e1-89a3-12a72adc87e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186605081}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7e758711-8a25-50c5-b452-853465d9bb2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-78560" :question/problem "Consider a system of $n$ linear equations in $n$ variables, written in matrix form as $D\\,s=p.$ Here, $D$ is the non-singular coefficient matrix of the system, $s$ is the column vector containing the variables, and $p$ is the column vector containing the constants. The unique solution of the system can be found using the method shown below:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D\\,s & =p \\\\ {D}^{-1}D\\,s & ={D}^{-1}\\,p \\\\ \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\color{blue}{\\phantom{{I}_{n}}}}s & ={D}^{-1}\\,p \\\\ \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\color{blue}{\\phantom{\\mathbf{s}}}} & ={D}^{-1}\\,p\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom and left to right, what are the missing parts of the derivation?" :question/worked-solution "Since $D$ is not singular, it must have an inverse ${D}^{-1}.$ Now, pre-multiplying both sides of the equation $D\\,s=p$ by ${D}^{-1},$ we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D\\,s & =p \\\\ {D}^{-1}D\\,s & ={D}^{-1}\\,p \\\\ {I}_{n}\\,s & ={D}^{-1}\\,p \\\\ s & ={D}^{-1}\\,p\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing parts are ${I}_{n}$ and $s.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186605128 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "310bce15-e43c-528d-8217-ba102a70523b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604790} {:answer/id #uuid "b5d67b9d-6611-540e-ae6f-d534a0f37bf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604924} {:answer/id #uuid "b9082aa5-ec48-58c9-8928-2e88cdfe35aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604929} {:answer/id #uuid "c8fa9282-f029-5abf-8c18-f33bbe57a9fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604949} {:answer/id #uuid "eb5b2e59-5e0f-59b3-b079-320a580ded37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604989}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604949} :answer-field/id #uuid "77a88b43-ca1c-5007-933a-1fa8bc9bcb09" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186605036}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "af30e6ef-e587-5850-99a9-71ce55884724" :question/math-academy-id "q-78545" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y+2z &=11 \\\\ 2x-7y+3z &=20 \\\\ x-3y+z &=8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n\\,{A}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -7 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ 20 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ 20 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=2,y=-1,z=3.$\n\nFinally, $x+y+z=2+(-1)+3=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186605132 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fae5a10-a649-5ec3-8215-5b9b8a753bd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604751}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604751} :answer-field/id #uuid "0de2af7f-836d-5e55-93b7-0ab30613ec80" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186605012} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dec76871-2a95-5b12-bc05-e8e25fcf595d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604977}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604977} :answer-field/id #uuid "929ea13b-a193-5da3-b3a7-de2f4d275ca7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186605045} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "014077de-494a-5527-96ca-19e9271095b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604732}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604732} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7085df5-8427-5de2-a57d-11f66cce199c" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186605061}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "bc4b0a42-7559-5451-9730-4eb942b49818" :question/math-academy-id "q-275783" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+2z &=4y-1 \\\\ x+2 &=y-z \\\\ y &=1+x+2z\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the solution $x=[x,y,z]^{T}$ of the system by computing the inverse of the coefficient matrix.\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "We organize the system so that it’s in the correct order first:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-4y+2z &=-1 \\\\ x-y+z &=-2 \\\\ -x+y-2z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix}-(-4)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{vmatrix}+2\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(2-1)+4(-2+1)+2(1-1) \\\\  & =2-4+0 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -6 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -6 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -6 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n \n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -6 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186605145 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19fe7f8d-0cbd-5f02-9e1e-85e1b327a514" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "${D}^{-1}$ and $D$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604770} {:answer/id #uuid "35440f05-53a6-5447-a858-890e9cfd9004" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "${D}^{-1}$ and ${D}^{-1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604795} {:answer/id #uuid "5f84c683-8397-5130-9b92-9ffa99a23516" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "${D}^{-1}$ and $x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604828} {:answer/id #uuid "616ffd53-46cc-54c1-99fc-92358c89bfc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "${D}^{-1}$ and ${I}_{n}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604831} {:answer/id #uuid "ca660ab8-95ee-54d6-9608-1376d33dab4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$D$ and $v$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604953}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604795} :answer-field/id #uuid "10867fbd-40d3-5bf4-921f-3fe1e1fb8c59" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186605013}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "eda9bc38-f2fb-500f-93d5-188f1df67a12" :question/math-academy-id "q-78558" :question/problem "Consider a system of $n$ linear equations in $n$ variables, written in matrix form as $D\\,x=v.$ Here, $D$ is the non-singular coefficient matrix of the system, $x$ is the column vector containing the variables, and $v$ is the column vector containing the constants. The unique solution of the system can be found using the method shown below:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D\\,x & =v \\\\ \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\color{blue}{\\phantom{{D}^{-1}}}}D\\,x & ={D}^{-1}\\,v \\\\ {I}_{n}\\,x & =\\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\color{blue}{\\phantom{{D}^{-1}}}}\\,v \\\\ x & ={D}^{-1}\\,v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom and left to right, what are the missing parts of the derivation?" :question/worked-solution "Since $D$ is not singular, it must have an inverse ${D}^{-1}.$ Now, pre-multiplying both sides of the equation $D\\,x=v$ by ${D}^{-1},$ we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D\\,x & =v \\\\ {D}^{-1}D\\,x & ={D}^{-1}v \\\\ {I}_{n}\\,x & ={D}^{-1}\\,v \\\\ x & ={D}^{-1}\\,v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing parts are ${D}^{-1}$ and ${D}^{-1}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186605843 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37b40480-6379-5bd4-afcb-90950f76139a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186605358} {:answer/id #uuid "43b41ec4-a1ce-56ba-b922-35dfb7650a33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186605375} {:answer/id #uuid "579e4072-0760-573d-ad3a-4252d637d7ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186605409} {:answer/id #uuid "ad5c18b2-d24a-523f-9284-7ca45d7690a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186605571} {:answer/id #uuid "f8634110-06b1-5692-82da-78a397a2b9cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186605701}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186605409} :answer-field/id #uuid "02ff21e8-13c8-5e18-aa6b-85cbe738d108" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186605717}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "30b9fe53-9d09-54e6-8339-965455cc4961" :question/math-academy-id "q-35301" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\text{dim}(\\text{Span}\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\})=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 9 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 6 & -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 6 & -12 \\\\ 6 & -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 6 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-6){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -18 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to basis vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns (or alternatively, it has exactly $3$ non-zero rows). \n\nTherefore, \n$$\n\\displaystyle \\text{dim}(\\text{Span}\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\})=3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186612408 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0da9b770-4a11-52a9-927d-fe96c8747178" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=11,\\,b=-5,\\,c=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611738} {:answer/id #uuid "2cb18601-9a02-5e1c-9279-64a01b06ec7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=-4,\\,b=11,\\,c=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611800} {:answer/id #uuid "3090a786-af3a-57a7-80ce-8e9c988194bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=-4,\\,b=5,\\,c=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611810} {:answer/id #uuid "d2c28dda-2655-5245-89c9-16ed610b6819" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=-4,\\,b=-5,\\,c=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612148} {:answer/id #uuid "fb6a3c5e-a742-55e0-860b-bf5a23863500" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=0,\\,b=-5,\\,c=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612243}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186612148} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e3db6f0-3dc5-5fb9-b8d8-ecf365eb7f0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612296}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "094bbee1-8c96-5483-9493-e0b570807e79" :question/math-academy-id "q-36182" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-4x+7y+z &=1 \\\\ 5x+2y-5z &=0 \\\\ 11x+3y+z &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}a & 7 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & b \\\\ 11 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ c \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 7 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 11 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 7 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 11 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-4,\\,b=-5,\\,c=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186612415 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bc5d67a-ad55-57b6-8e82-4e3e891206e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=3,\\,b=2,\\,c=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611798} {:answer/id #uuid "58e36130-1541-502e-820c-1d39b9a604d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=7,\\,c=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611888} {:answer/id #uuid "91dce036-1bc4-54cd-b544-0fff343f518f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=2,\\,b=7,\\,c=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612002} {:answer/id #uuid "a849e88b-b3fb-543c-ae58-9b8b3bc87fee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=7,\\,b=2,\\,c=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612056} {:answer/id #uuid "cc76838f-aea8-5eb5-87b4-7f76baf755dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=7,\\,c=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612126}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186612002} :answer-field/id #uuid "6785a910-2277-5c34-ab67-32d0960c7358" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612309}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1b38ff25-ea3c-5c42-a3ea-dc98a54a3e91" :question/math-academy-id "q-10005" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+3y+z &=6 \\\\ 4x+7y+2z &=0 \\\\ 3x+y+z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}a & 3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & b & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=2,\\,b=7,\\,c=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186612436 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f074f3d0-cf6d-52ad-9396-e358f8dcb583" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612215}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186612215} :answer-field/id #uuid "9529aede-2f35-5e55-ab84-079a233be8ed" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612339} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "869a074e-87a9-5700-805a-44e072fd18ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611982}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186611982} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9b00621-281f-5a93-83e3-8ab9332fa7f7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612358} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e3df0d5-3cce-543c-8674-88acc17d49e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611766}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186611766} :answer-field/id #uuid "d909e574-f02f-5a3f-8c24-59b659dcc11e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612379} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b29b25a9-03d8-514c-90f4-dbe7b6c3be98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612071}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186612071} :answer-field/id #uuid "e71d1853-e8cf-584b-a606-9235871b3686" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612387}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5b9fd4ac-7545-5ee9-99f4-ab2e0ba107d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-275512" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3z-6x-4 &=0 \\\\ 2y-x-3z-1 &=0 \\\\ 5y+2x-9 &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $-6$ | {{field-1}} | $3$ |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | $4$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $-1$ | $2$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | $1$ |  | . |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} | $5$ | $0$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-6x+0y+3z &=4 \\\\ -x+2y-3z &=1 \\\\ 2x+5y+0z &=6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186612448 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3631a5fa-5e55-558e-8872-399877d753dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611818}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186611818} :answer-field/id #uuid "38985f52-1497-5d07-b169-66bf991e1442" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612282} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0417e0a-596a-5dfd-bec9-d099be2a0dbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612105}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186612105} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e5d273e-a334-5366-9bc8-2b62109c6126" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612313} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "324db564-ad58-58d9-8da4-a0b8891ea682" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186611814}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186611814} :answer-field/id #uuid "7661a73a-740a-5cbf-9c4d-ae0c8469ff0d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612320} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0aac2f3-2186-5a39-a0d9-20ac913d4966" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612139}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186612139} :answer-field/id #uuid "aaa2a814-5220-5d51-8326-676df3b0f6c5" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612348}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "761c774a-fba6-5d9d-8799-397695349ab3" :question/math-academy-id "q-316997" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4z+2x+y-1 &=0 \\\\ y+2z+3x &=2 \\\\ x+5z+2y-3 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $2$ | {{field-1}} | $4$ |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | $1$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | {{field-2}} | $1$ | $2$ |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | $2$ |  | . |\n|  |  | $1$ | $2$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+y+4z &=1 \\\\ 3x+y+2z &=2 \\\\ x+2y+5z &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186619714 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4cfe39db-acc2-5ffc-8320-dabe1df0cc38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619287} {:answer/id #uuid "c09f0cab-9825-596c-9cda-7c5f7162be64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619485} {:answer/id #uuid "c22c590c-5165-56fa-bcf7-d2bb803a74d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619490} {:answer/id #uuid "eab7d483-435a-5eb7-ae5f-bb780482526a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619552} {:answer/id #uuid "f3cff2cf-4658-5bb7-b160-3527896c02c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619568}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186619287} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1221b2c-7e3a-502f-92aa-1fb5a7f3c23b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619696}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "05d0ccda-149f-5815-a2fa-d34fa1d78c34" :question/math-academy-id "q-78556" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-y-5z &=2 \\\\ x+3y+9z &=-2 \\\\ x+4y+15z &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n\\,{A}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -5 & 6 \\\\ -6 & 5 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 15\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -5 & 6 \\\\ -6 & 5 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=4,y=-2,z=0.$\n\nFinally, $x+y+z=4+(-2)+0=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186619719 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "670cd53e-6408-5341-a434-723e0ecd2caa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619328} {:answer/id #uuid "94316272-54f3-5bc8-90dc-a33a57cf576a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619403} {:answer/id #uuid "c39ac04b-3124-5255-bbd1-f74eeb814ffe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619492} {:answer/id #uuid "c6c1c992-9929-5f51-8261-e5202ccd0a1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619498} {:answer/id #uuid "ffe88724-b341-5237-bd7c-1271937eee7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619591}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186619403} :answer-field/id #uuid "e60e94cf-0253-5991-9a4c-c57043e1437f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619698}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0e06e055-0f83-5ee9-a424-a115e878284a" :question/math-academy-id "q-78539" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y-z &=2 \\\\ -x+y-4z &=-2 \\\\ 2x+y-2z &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, what is the value of $xyz?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n\\,{A}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -10 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -10 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=-1,y=5,z=2.$\n\nFinally, $xyz=(-1)\\cdot 5\\cdot 2=-10.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186637238 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "643195b8-5f3c-5dec-a199-1d4e1566d7c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636844} {:answer/id #uuid "ab69d199-b8fe-570c-872d-ce2b5bd7a3b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636969} {:answer/id #uuid "bbe6b9bb-289d-560f-a1f6-fa661bc9a8a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636999} {:answer/id #uuid "db4125cf-daf8-57ba-ab40-6725dd625804" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637051} {:answer/id #uuid "ff6a29d3-f315-52df-9f3d-fdc297bf21be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637116}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186637116} :answer-field/id #uuid "f566f2c2-8864-5e73-a36e-4bddc02ba233" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186637223}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0b137dad-7db4-50cb-b5c8-f93f31b8129d" :question/math-academy-id "q-18253" :question/problem "Given that the determinant of \n$$\n\\displaystyle \\begin{bmatrix}1-2p & 4 & 2p+1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$ \nis $-126,$  find the value of $p.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}1-2p & 4 & 2p+1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -2 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & =(1-2p)\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{vmatrix}-4\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 2\\end{vmatrix}+(2p+1)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 6 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(1-2p)\\cdot 6-4\\cdot 2+(2p+1)\\cdot (-20) \\\\  & =6-12p-8-40p-20 \\\\  & =-52p-22\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $-126,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-52p-22 & =-126 \\\\ -52p & =-104 \\\\ p & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186642291 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "007572d5-2ce0-5624-a3db-b61acb9c8c59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+z\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186641818} {:answer/id #uuid "a1db24c1-d882-593b-a6eb-c15a5b698e5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+z\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642077} {:answer/id #uuid "b1a600ee-6399-5e90-8b2b-00bd828a3cfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642093} {:answer/id #uuid "c6bf4589-5d97-5049-b122-349409ad9c2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+z\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642119} {:answer/id #uuid "f839e947-688e-5bbe-a22b-3681cef97055" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+z\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642187}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186642093} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f5a92c6-9883-5cdc-9699-ed459edf8336" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642240}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "04fe0322-b2bc-5fa8-a456-3a2fec189434" :question/math-academy-id "q-131506" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-9 & 8 & 6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -9 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 9\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "The system corresponding to $M$ is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-9x+8y+6z &=1 \\\\ 0x+2y-9z &=-3 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=9\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince there are no such numbers $x,y,z$ that form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=9,$ we can conclude that our system has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186642307 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10e0a1ce-fb3d-5959-9754-60384a5c2762" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{y}{2} \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186641848} {:answer/id #uuid "5353ee39-6188-5e67-ab0b-4d1f690e47c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3+2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186641957} {:answer/id #uuid "87a4a255-4fb4-5f02-9fea-0e5ff192cd90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642041} {:answer/id #uuid "bd3373af-51e0-5b24-b6c7-ef393c877d3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ \\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642102} {:answer/id #uuid "c980099c-8f7b-5947-b9bd-2307e49d9d71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642122}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186641957} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4cef5ee-e616-5845-861c-fd824bd96d1b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642271}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3c835c9f-7022-5bdf-9b7d-f5a905e41275" :question/math-academy-id "q-42062" :question/problem "Solve the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-6y &=9 \\\\ -2x+4y &=-6 \\\\ x-2y &=3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & -6 & 9 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & -6 & 9 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now  \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$ and we have one free variable, $y.$ That means we need to find $x$  in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=3+2y \\\\ y &=y,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3+2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186642313 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "195e4881-a43e-5d21-a226-65f48e3b30ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1+z \\\\ 1-z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186641864} {:answer/id #uuid "329dc6cd-7d48-541d-9b08-6b334a27cfff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1+z \\\\ -1-z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186641911} {:answer/id #uuid "588ffac7-61f6-5425-b926-89594f1ea5ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1+z \\\\ -2-z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186641966} {:answer/id #uuid "b41a3ad7-e755-59ad-9862-845761301739" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642095} {:answer/id #uuid "d77fb993-a237-58e2-9382-a65cb976797b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1+z \\\\ -z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642147}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186641864} :answer-field/id #uuid "742dca4d-9f70-503c-8a37-968e1cf348e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642249}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4ede18d8-a6be-5c44-904c-511ce67bbd52" :question/math-academy-id "q-20972" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the matrix $M$ is already in row echelon form. The system corresponding to $M$ is \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+z &=3 \\\\ y+z &=1 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of just two equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+z &=3 \\\\ y+z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ To do this, we apply the back substitution. \n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+z=1\\,⇒\\,y=1-z\n$$\n\nand substituting this into the first equation get \n\n$$\nx+2(1-z)+z=3\\,⇒\\,x=1+z.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=1+z \\\\ y &=1-z \\\\ z &=z,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1+z \\\\ 1-z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186642334 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10178cdb-69fa-5b2a-87d7-4e3e844e1b47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-1 & 0 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186641847} {:answer/id #uuid "421b7867-4200-5819-9238-7136a1c4d9be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186641938} {:answer/id #uuid "49200c6e-3e97-5014-83b0-1e6b62f5e2df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186641947} {:answer/id #uuid "cda0ee4b-1800-5a95-b122-0c8626c118b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642132} {:answer/id #uuid "f59049b7-43a1-5e0b-a7d0-f0062677fba7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642180}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186642180} :answer-field/id #uuid "411ad6a3-6b91-5428-95f4-86008b87a0a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642228}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "789a4978-8190-50d7-8f55-d4c03ce00d60" :question/math-academy-id "q-37651" :question/problem "Consider the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+3{x}_{3} &=2 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+12{x}_{3} &=6 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}-9{x}_{3} &=-2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for the system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-1 & 0 & 3 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 12 & 6 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -9 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-1 & 0 & 3 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 12 & 6 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -9 & -2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 12 & 6 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -9 & -2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -9 & -2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186642470 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05cd2126-e761-5314-bbea-aa545e9ae770" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 11 \\\\ -8 & -12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642462} {:answer/id #uuid "b446047d-7f98-5b49-a508-ba34a38f61c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 11 \\\\ -8 & -13\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642483} {:answer/id #uuid "b95c3c6e-da6d-5fd1-a363-8125705cc5f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 11 \\\\ -8 & -14\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642487} {:answer/id #uuid "bf5b5050-4d7c-5cba-b724-c4acf59ead91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 10 \\\\ -9 & -13\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642489} {:answer/id #uuid "e053450e-2ab1-5c00-9fad-2b72e66995a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 12 \\\\ -7 & -13\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642494}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186642487} :answer-field/id #uuid "cade34c2-3d50-5b92-bc18-cdfd23007f72" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642491}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "621bedd0-869f-57e4-93cc-a8fa0ae4d51f" :question/problem "Find $AB$, if\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix and $B$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $A$ and $3$ rows in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}={AB}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, \\\\ & \\,-1=1\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 11 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, \\\\ & \\,11=1\\cdot 3+(-2)\\cdot (-2)+1\\cdot 4 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 11 \\\\ -8 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, \\\\ & \\,-8=(-2)\\cdot 2+4\\cdot (-1)+0\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 11 \\\\ -8 & -14\\end{bmatrix}, \\\\ & \\,-14=(-2)\\cdot 3+4\\cdot (-2)+0\\cdot 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$$\n\\displaystyle AB=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 11 \\\\ -8 & -14\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186642471 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f4c03f8-675d-5c46-9956-a4354ef7bd07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & -5 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642475} {:answer/id #uuid "9683bd22-3ed4-5749-8bf4-9bd3fea8fcf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642480} {:answer/id #uuid "b9194a14-8a73-5358-9c23-396a77580c0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & -4 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642485} {:answer/id #uuid "bdeccf2c-3aa9-5dbe-98c8-46794507e347" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-11 & -4 \\\\ -3 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642488} {:answer/id #uuid "f722f631-e17c-572b-a43d-cdc965613256" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & -4 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642496}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186642496} :answer-field/id #uuid "37bfe405-d85d-5786-a704-c56dba09f12f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642467}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "682f503a-7bda-54cb-a214-85f0337b0942" :question/problem "If\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$E=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$F=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nthen $EF=$" :question/worked-solution "Here, $E$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix and $F$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $4$ columns in $E$ and $4$ rows in $F,$ so $E$ and $F$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{E}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{F}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 2}={EF}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $EF,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, \\\\ & \\,-10=(-1)\\cdot 3+(-2)\\cdot 0+1\\cdot (-4)+1\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & -4 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, \\\\ & \\,-4=(-1)\\cdot 3+(-2)\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & -4 \\\\ -3 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, \\\\ & \\,-3=(-2)\\cdot 3+3\\cdot 0+0\\cdot (-4)+(-1)\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & -4 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}, \\\\ & \\,-2=(-2)\\cdot 3+3\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot (-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$$\n\\displaystyle EF=\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & -4 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186642479 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52bb132c-2bbf-5ace-8c8f-de256c2eb53e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642468} {:answer/id #uuid "68d82f83-b7bb-58c5-86c3-f04d6d9c290a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 11\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642472} {:answer/id #uuid "7596babc-6db1-50c1-8a27-134740047098" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 11\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642476} {:answer/id #uuid "b4c5a46b-2d0a-5b54-9af3-4e5b9e449463" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642484} {:answer/id #uuid "cc0e645a-86e0-5743-9e79-9cd7fc2e5e43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 11\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642492}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186642468} :answer-field/id #uuid "6de4420e-51ad-522a-90c4-89e34f50924e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642473}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "94857107-c897-51f4-8aee-36e2b50b1efe" :question/problem "Find $XY$,  if\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$X=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$Y=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -5 \\\\ -3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Here, $X$ is a $1\\times 3$ matrix and $Y$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $X$ and $3$ rows in $Y,$ so $X$ and $Y$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{X}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{Y}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}={XY}_{1\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $XY,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -5 \\\\ -3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, \\\\ & \\,8=(-2)\\cdot (-4)+(-1)\\cdot (-3)+(-1)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -5 \\\\ -3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 10\\end{bmatrix}, \\\\ & \\,10=(-2)\\cdot (-5)+(-1)\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$$\n\\displaystyle XY=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186642482 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "096dfddb-d40e-540c-a5e4-9ec9ea2ec7a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 6 \\\\ -12 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642463} {:answer/id #uuid "27f18784-4500-57e7-95b1-512450bcdad6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 7 \\\\ -11 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642465} {:answer/id #uuid "5e6e97b1-30f0-5cbb-982c-16a2416962a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 7 \\\\ -11 & -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642469} {:answer/id #uuid "c173493f-f21c-52a3-ba71-0f2173f2e025" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 8 \\\\ -10 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642490} {:answer/id #uuid "d4b5eb28-c9cb-58ee-a0c5-a364992acce6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 7 \\\\ -11 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642493}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186642490} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f63b45f-39fc-55c1-a51b-567ea975b6ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642478}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b00e7f3e-2523-5d0a-a40a-274064ef9979" :question/problem "Find $AB$, if\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix and $B$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $A$ and $3$ rows in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}={AB}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, \\\\ & \\,4=4\\cdot (-1)+0\\cdot 5+(-4)\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 8 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, \\\\ & \\,8=4\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 4+(-4)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 8 \\\\ -10 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, \\\\ & \\,-10=1\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 5+2\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 8 \\\\ -10 & -5\\end{bmatrix}, \\\\ & \\,-5=1\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 4+2\\cdot (-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$$\n\\displaystyle AB=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 8 \\\\ -10 & -5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186642486 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "116d6830-b759-5827-938e-755cbdea6732" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 7 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642464} {:answer/id #uuid "316b5c18-fb8b-556b-86bd-bf3f04f390b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 6 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642466} {:answer/id #uuid "6e8992e1-e263-5d99-a404-d8a59bf2c45a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 