-stacked\">\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$Q=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$PQ=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>{{field-2}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-3}}</td><td>{{field-4}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-5}}</td><td>{{field-6}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Here, $P$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix and $Q$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix.  \n\nThere is $1$ column in matrix $P$ and $1$ row in matrix $Q$, so the product is well defined:\n\n$$\n{P}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{Q}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={PQ}_{3\\times 2}\n$$\n\nComputing the product, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}PQ & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}(-7)\\cdot (-4) & (-7)\\cdot 1 \\\\ (-5)\\cdot (-4) & (-5)\\cdot 1 \\\\ 7\\cdot (-4) & 7\\cdot 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}28 & -7 \\\\ 20 & -5 \\\\ -28 & 7\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186643266 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32e773a3-3fea-5e4d-b382-bd51abf2672a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-24 & -4 \\\\ -24 & -4 \\\\ -24 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643257} {:answer/id #uuid "4eeb160c-0011-56a7-a78e-f31cd5fa91cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "Undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643260} {:answer/id #uuid "6fa12642-dcec-5ff6-afce-8ca990526cbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-36 & 6 \\\\ 24 & -4 \\\\ 42 & -7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643268} {:answer/id #uuid "872d5a98-acf2-59ef-8c69-b77336b5a675" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}24 & -4 \\\\ 24 & -4 \\\\ 24 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643276} {:answer/id #uuid "bfdbf2cb-1cd5-512d-a13f-2864ce1094cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}36 & 6 \\\\ -24 & -4 \\\\ -42 & -7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643285}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186643268} :answer-field/id #uuid "de1dbe14-4f16-549c-b1de-43e0c3781011" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643293}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "681cfd4c-14bd-5bf1-82a9-23519fd5b033" :question/problem "Find $PQ,$ if\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$Q=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Here, $P$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix and $Q$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix.  \n\nThere is $1$ column in matrix $P$ and $1$ row in matrix $Q$, so the product is well defined:\n\n$$\n{P}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{Q}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={PQ}_{3\\times 2}\n$$\n\nComputing the product, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}PQ & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6\\cdot (-6) & 6\\cdot 1 \\\\ (-4)\\cdot (-6) & (-4)\\cdot 1 \\\\ (-7)\\cdot (-6) & (-7)\\cdot 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-36 & 6 \\\\ 24 & -4 \\\\ 42 & -7\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
